package encode

import "core/slice"
import "std/image/color"
import "std/image/pixels"
import "std/image/shared/binary"
import "std/image/shared/scratch"

// JPEG XL encoder: pure Dodo, no allocation. Lossless (the default) is
// integer-only with byte-identical output on every target; lossy
// (EncodeOptions.lossless = false) writes a VarDCT frame at a Butteraugli
// distance.
//
// Design (lossless)
//
// Output is one lossless modular frame (not XYB) as a bare codestream, or in
// the ISOBMFF container (signature, ftyp, optional jxll/Exif/xml boxes, then
// jxlc) when asked for or when EXIF or XMP is attached; an ICC profile goes
// into the codestream. Samples keep their precision: U8 and U16 become 8 and
// 16-bit integer samples; F16 and F32 become 16 and 32-bit float samples
// whose bit patterns are coded exactly.
// Alpha is an extra channel; premultiplied input is stored unchanged and
// flagged alpha_associated.
//
// Bitstream: 256x256 groups. A single-group image is one section. Larger
// images get a TOC with LfGlobal (MA tree, entropy codes, palette and the
// global transform header), empty LF group and HfGlobal sections, and one
// section per group with its rectangle of every channel. One global tree
// and one set of clustered entropy codes serve all groups; they come from a
// first pass that counts symbols over the whole image, and a second pass
// writes each group independently. Runs of equal residuals become LZ77
// copies at distance 1 (RLE). Channels whose samples share a factor (8-bit
// data * 257, 12-bit data * 16) code residuals divided by it through the
// tree leaf multiplier.
//
// Entropy coding (entropy.dodo, ans.dodo, prefix.dodo): effort 1 counts
// hybrid integer tokens 4/2/0 and writes prefix codes. Effort 2+ counts
// finer tokens (5/2/2, which keep enough of every residual of 8 and
// 16-bit samples), clusters the contexts on their 4/2/0 projection, picks
// each cluster's hybrid integer configuration from 26 candidates by
// estimated size, and then codes the set with ANS (12-bit distributions
// stored with the flat, small or general method at the cheapest precision
// shift, alias tables, a 32-bit rANS state per stream with 16-bit flushes)
// when that is estimated smaller than prefix codes, likewise for the tree.
// ANS streams are written in reverse: each stream's tokens are buffered
// (two words each) and coded when the stream ends.
//
// ICC profiles (icc.dodo) are embedded after the image header with
// libjxl's predictive ICC encoding (header prediction, tag table commands,
// type and XYZ shortcuts, shuffled mluc text, numeric prediction of curves
// and CLUTs), LZ77 and per-cluster prefix codes over 41 byte contexts. The
// encoded profile is regenerated on every pass rather than stored, so its
// working memory is fixed and carved from the histogram scratch before the
// image passes start.
//
// Effort:
//   1: fjxl-like: YCoCg for RGB, the clamped gradient predictor, one context
//      per channel, at most 8 prefix codes (4/2/0 hybrid integers).
//   2: palette (up to 1024 colors), the best of three color transforms, the
//      best of gradient/W/N per channel, contexts from the local gradients
//      W-NW and NW-N (and the previous channel's residual), up to 32
//      clustered codes with tuned hybrid integers, ANS when smaller (some
//      precision shifts). Choices are estimated by coding sample bands of
//      the image with the real model.
//   3+: nine color transforms, more predictors including the weighted
//      (self-correcting) predictor with contexts on its error, four times
//      the sample, and every ANS precision shift.
//
// Memory: encode_scratch_size() bytes of scratch, carved into the i32
// planes of one group (all channels; 256x256 at most), the context
// histograms (256 contexts x 288 symbols), cluster sums, prefix code
// tables, the palette hash and the TOC sizes (4 bytes per group); effort 2+
// adds ANS tables (32 clusters x 9 KiB) and a token buffer of 8 bytes per
// sample of one group. Planes and tokens are bounded by the group size, so
// scratch stays between about 0.4 and 1.5 MiB at effort 1 and 0.7 and 4
// MiB at effort 2+, for any image. max_encoded_size() bounds the output
// (max_encoded_size_with_metadata() with metadata and ICC profile).
//
// Design (lossy, vd_*.dodo)
//
// One VarDCT frame in XYB (image metadata xyb_encoded; the color encoding
// names the source's space, which the decoder converts back to). Samples
// are linearized with the header's transfer curve (sRGB, linear, BT.709,
// PQ, HLG, power laws), moved to sRGB primaries when needed, and turned into
// XYB by libjxl's opsin matrix, bias and cube root; float and 16-bit
// sources keep their precision up to that point. With an ICC profile
// (vd_icc.dodo) the samples reach linear sRGB through the profile instead,
// as a color management system reads it (its AToB lookup table, else its
// matrix/TRC or gray curve; relative colorimetric via the D50 connection
// space), and the header embeds the profile as libjxl does: decoders with
// color management render XYB into it, std/image/jxl into sRGB. Per frame: a global quant
// scale and LF quant from the distance (libjxl's formulas), default
// dequantization matrices, x_qm_scale from the distance, Gaborish (effort 2+,
// distance above 0.5) and EPF iterations (0 to 3 by distance) signalled as
// applied. Per 256x256 group, analyzed with an 8-pixel border so results do
// not depend on group order: the adaptive quant field (libjxl's masking
// model) from the original XYB, inverse Gaborish (libjxl's 5x5 kernel),
// then per 64x64 tile the varblock search (effort 3+: libjxl's entropy plus
// information-loss estimate, merging DCT8 into 16x8, 16x16, 32x16, 32x32
// and, at effort 7+, 64x32 and 64x64), the quant field per varblock,
// chroma-from-luma factors fitted per tile (least squares, libjxl's
// weighting), and quantization with libjxl's dead zones and per-block quant
// adjustment (effort 3+). The LF image (one value per 8x8 block, the
// lowest frequencies of each varblock folded back) is quantized with LF
// chroma-from-luma, and with the HF metadata (chroma-from-luma tiles,
// varblock types and quants, EPF sharpness) coded per LF group in modular
// streams with their own trees. HF coefficients use the default block
// context map, the decoder's nonzero-count prediction and contexts and the
// natural coefficient orders; their tokens (counted as hybrid integers
// 4/1/0) are clustered into at most 32 histograms with an MTF + LZ77 coded
// context map. Alpha stays lossless in the modular stream (global tree and
// codes, one stream per group). Entropy coding follows the lossless
// effort levels: effort 1 writes prefix codes (with runs of more than 4
// equal HF tokens as LZ77 copies); effort 2+ tunes each cluster's hybrid
// integer configuration and codes with ANS when that is estimated smaller,
// for the HF code and every modular stream (LF image, HF metadata, alpha),
// with HF copies only for runs of more than 96 tokens.
//
// Two passes, group by group: the first analyzes each LF group's groups,
// writes the LF group and counts the HF tokens; after the HF code is built
// the second analyzes every group again (reusing the first pass's
// decisions when the image is one LF group, up to 2048x2048) and writes
// its tokens. Every HF token goes through VdHfCoder.token in vd_hf.dodo,
// the single seam to the entropy coder.
//
// Lossy memory: encode_scratch_size() is about
//   2.7 MiB fixed (HF histograms 7426 contexts x 64 symbols x 4 bytes,
//     dequantization weights, orders, the modular coder)
//   + 18 g^2 bytes for the group (XYB planes with an 8-pixel border,
//     quantized coefficients), plus 8 g^2 more at effort 3+ (masking
//     field), g = min(256, image side rounded up to 8)
//   + 28 b^2 bytes for the LF group (LF image, metadata, block info),
//     b = min(256, image side in blocks)
//   + 1 KiB (8-bit) or 256 KiB (16-bit and half-float) linearization table
//   + 4 bytes per alpha sample of one group
//   + at effort 2+: 288 KiB of ANS tables (32 clusters x 4608 u16; shared
//     by the LF group streams and the HF code), 288 KiB more for alpha's
//     code, and 24 b^2 + b^2 / 8 bytes of ANS tokens for the larger LF
//     group stream (HF and alpha group streams buffer theirs in the HF
//     histograms, idle by then),
// at most about 9 MiB whatever the image size (5 MiB for 1366x768 at
// effort 2). max_encoded_size() is a true bound (31 bits per HF
// coefficient, 40 per LF and metadata symbol, the alpha samples' lossless
// bound, and the coding overhead).

// Default effort for EncodeOptions.new().
pub const DEFAULT_EFFORT: u32 = 2

// Default Butteraugli distance of lossy encoding (cjxl's default, about
// quality 90).
pub const DEFAULT_DISTANCE: f32 = 1.0

// Encoder settings.
pub struct EncodeOptions {
    // 1 (fastest) to 9. Lossless: values above 3 currently behave like 3,
    // 0 like 1. Lossy: 1 DCT8 with uniform quantization; 2 adds adaptive
    // quantization, inverse Gaborish and chroma-from-luma; 3-6 add the
    // varblock search (DCT8 to DCT32 and rectangles) and per-block quant
    // adjustment; 7-9 also try 64x64 varblocks.
    pub effort: u32
    // Lossless modular coding (the default). When false, a lossy VarDCT
    // frame in XYB is written at `distance`; alpha stays lossless.
    pub lossless: bool
    // Target Butteraugli distance of lossy coding: 1.0 is visually
    // lossless, 0.5 very high quality, 3 to 8 small files. Clamped to
    // 0.05..25; zero or less means lossless. distance_from_quality() maps
    // a 0..100 quality the way cjxl does.
    pub distance: f32
    // Wrap the codestream in the ISOBMFF container. Implied when metadata
    // is attached (encode_with_metadata).
    pub container: bool
    // Color description written as the JPEG XL color encoding: CICP
    // primaries and transfer (sRGB, linear, BT.709/601/2020 curves, PQ, HLG,
    // DCI, power-law gamma; BT.709, BT.2020, Display P3, DCI-P3 or custom
    // chromaticities). Unrepresentable values fall back to sRGB. Ignored
    // when an ICC profile is embedded (Metadata.icc).
    pub color: color.ColorInfo
    pub orientation: color.Orientation

    pub fn new() -> EncodeOptions {
        return EncodeOptions { effort: DEFAULT_EFFORT, lossless: true, distance: DEFAULT_DISTANCE, container: false, color: color.ColorInfo.srgb(), orientation: color.Orientation.Identity }
    }
    // Lossy settings at Butteraugli distance `distance`.
    pub fn lossy(distance: f32) -> EncodeOptions {
        options := EncodeOptions.new()
        options.lossless = false
        options.distance = distance
        return options
    }
    fn is_lossy(&self) -> bool {
        return !self.lossless && (self.distance > 0.0 || !(self.distance == self.distance))
    }
}

// Metadata stored with the image: EXIF and XMP in container boxes, the ICC
// profile in the codestream. Kept apart from EncodeOptions so the options
// hold no borrows.
pub struct Metadata {
    // EXIF payload starting at the TIFF header ("II*\0" or "MM\0*"), or
    // with a leading "Exif\0\0"; stored in an "Exif" box. Empty for none.
    pub exif: &[u8]
    // XMP packet, stored in an "xml " box. Empty for none.
    pub xmp: &[u8]
    // ICC profile embedded in the image header (entropy coded, see
    // icc.dodo); it then describes the colors instead of
    // EncodeOptions.color. Must be an RGB profile for RGB(A) images and a
    // gray one for gray(+alpha) images (else Unsupported). Lossy encoding
    // converts the samples to XYB through the profile, which must then be
    // a matrix/TRC profile (colorants and rTRC/gTRC/bTRC) or a gray kTRC
    // profile with the XYZ connection space (else Unsupported; profiles
    // that only have lookup tables are not supported); see vd_icc.dodo.
    // icc_usable() checks both. Empty for none; it does not need the
    // container.
    pub icc: &[u8]

    pub fn new(exif: &[u8], xmp: &[u8]) -> Metadata from(exif, xmp) {
        return Metadata { exif: exif, xmp: xmp, icc: &exif[..0] }
    }
    pub fn with_icc(exif: &[u8], xmp: &[u8], icc: &[u8]) -> Metadata from(exif, xmp, icc) {
        return Metadata { exif: exif, xmp: xmp, icc: icc }
    }
}

// Layout and modelling decisions for one encode.
struct Plan {
    width: usize
    height: usize
    // Source channels (1 to 4) and color channels (1 or 3).
    channels: usize
    color_channels: usize
    alpha: bool
    sample: u32
    bits: u32
    float: bool
    premultiplied: bool
    // Reversible color transform type (0..41) or -1.
    rct: i32
    // Palette colors, 0 for none.
    palette: usize
    // Channels of the modular image after transforms (palette: meta + index).
    modular_channels: usize
    predictors: [5]u32
    // Predictor fixed for correctness (mixed-sign float channels).
    locked: [5]bool
    // Per source channel: a common factor of every sample (usually 1).
    source_factors: [4]u32
    groups_x: usize
    groups_y: usize
    lf_groups: usize
    effort: u32
    lz77: bool
    min_length: usize
    // Use activity contexts (effort 2+).
    contexts: bool
    // The chroma subtrees may test the previous channel's residual.
    refs: bool
}

fn new_plan(width: u32, height: u32, layout: &pixels.Layout, effort: u32) -> Plan {
    channels := layout.channel_count()
    sample := layout.sample_code()
    bits := 8u32
    if sample == pixels.SAMPLE_U16 || sample == pixels.SAMPLE_F16 {
        bits = 16
    } else if sample == pixels.SAMPLE_F32 {
        bits = 32
    }
    color_channels := 1usize
    if channels >= 3 {
        color_channels = 3
    }
    e := effort
    if e == 0 {
        e = 1
    }
    if e > 3 {
        e = 3
    }
    w := width as usize
    h := height as usize
    rct := -1i32
    if color_channels == 3 && sample != pixels.SAMPLE_F32 {
        rct = 6
    }
    return Plan { width: w, height: h, channels: channels, color_channels: color_channels, alpha: channels == 2 || channels == 4, sample: sample, bits: bits, float: sample >= pixels.SAMPLE_F16, premultiplied: layout.premultiplied && (channels == 2 || channels == 4), rct: rct, palette: 0, modular_channels: channels, predictors: [5u32; 5], locked: [false; 5], source_factors: [1u32; 4], groups_x: (w + 255) / 256, groups_y: (h + 255) / 256, lf_groups: ((w + 2047) / 2048) * ((h + 2047) / 2048), effort: e, lz77: true, min_length: 7, contexts: e >= 2 && sample != pixels.SAMPLE_F32, refs: e >= 2 && sample != pixels.SAMPLE_F32 }
}

fn group_count(width: usize, height: usize) -> usize {
    return ((width + 255) / 256) * ((height + 255) / 256)
}

// TOC entries: one for a single-group image, else LfGlobal, the LF groups,
// HfGlobal and every group.
fn toc_entries(width: usize, height: usize) -> usize {
    groups := group_count(width, height)
    if groups == 1 {
        return 1
    }
    return 2 + ((width + 2047) / 2048) * ((height + 2047) / 2048) + groups
}

fn check_size(width: u32, height: u32) -> void!pixels.Error {
    if width == 0 || height == 0 {
        return err(pixels.Error.Malformed)
    }
    return binary.check_dimensions(width, height)
}

// Bytes of container boxes before the codestream.
fn container_prefix(options: &EncodeOptions, exif: &[u8], xmp: &[u8], codestream_bound: usize, level10: bool) -> usize!pixels.Error {
    if !options.container && exif.len == 0 && xmp.len == 0 {
        return ok(0)
    }
    total := 12usize + 20
    if level10 {
        total += 9
    }
    if exif.len > 0 {
        total = pixels.checked(1, total, exif.len + 12)?
    }
    if xmp.len > 0 {
        total = pixels.checked(1, total, xmp.len + 8)?
    }
    if codestream_bound + 8 > 0xFFFFFFFF {
        total += 16
    } else {
        total += 8
    }
    return ok(total)
}

// Level 5 allows integer samples up to 16 bits and moderate dimensions;
// anything else announces level 10 in the container.
fn needs_level10(width: u32, height: u32, layout: &pixels.Layout) -> bool {
    if layout.sample_code() == pixels.SAMPLE_F32 {
        return true
    }
    return width > 262144 || height > 262144 || width as u64 * height as u64 > 268435456
}

// Worst-case bits per sample: a 15-bit prefix code (or ANS with its 16-bit
// flushes, which never cost more than 16 bits per token) plus the hybrid
// integer extra bits of the largest residual (8 or 16-bit samples after a
// color transform give residuals below 2^(bits + 2), with margin for the
// weighted predictor), or 30 bits for 32-bit float patterns.
fn sample_bound_bits(layout: &pixels.Layout) -> usize {
    code := layout.sample_code()
    if code == pixels.SAMPLE_U8 {
        return 16 + 8 + 2
    }
    if code == pixels.SAMPLE_F32 {
        return 16 + 30
    }
    return 16 + 16 + 2
}

fn codestream_bound(width: u32, height: u32, layout: &pixels.Layout) -> usize!pixels.Error {
    check_size(width, height)?
    w := width as usize
    h := height as usize
    samples := pixels.checked(binary.pixel_count(width, height)?, layout.channel_count(), MAX_PALETTE * 4)?
    data := pixels.checked(samples, sample_bound_bits(layout), 7)? / 8
    // Headers, tree, codes and per-section padding (and ANS states).
    overhead := pixels.checked(toc_entries(w, h), 8, 65536)?
    return pixels.checked(1, data, overhead)
}

// An upper bound on the bytes an embedded ICC profile of `length` bytes
// adds to the output: the predicted stream has at most 2 * length + 64
// bytes, each coded in at most 22 bits (LZ77 copies cost less per byte),
// plus the code spec.
pub fn icc_bound(length: usize) -> usize!pixels.Error {
    if length == 0 {
        return ok(0)
    }
    return pixels.checked(length, 6, 16384 + 192)
}

// An upper bound on the bytes encode() writes for this image and options.
// It is a worst case (about 3 bytes per 8-bit sample); typical output is
// far smaller, and encode() reports BufferTooSmall rather than overrunning a
// smaller buffer.
pub fn max_encoded_size(width: u32, height: u32, layout: &pixels.Layout, options: &EncodeOptions) -> usize!pixels.Error {
    if options.is_lossy() {
        md := Metadata.new(b"", b"")
        return vd_max_encoded_size(width, height, layout, options, &md)
    }
    bound := codestream_bound(width, height, layout)?
    prefix := container_prefix(options, b"", b"", bound, needs_level10(width, height, layout))?
    return pixels.checked(1, bound, prefix)
}

// max_encoded_size() including the metadata boxes and the ICC profile.
pub fn max_encoded_size_with_metadata(width: u32, height: u32, layout: &pixels.Layout, options: &EncodeOptions, metadata: &Metadata) -> usize!pixels.Error {
    if options.is_lossy() {
        return vd_max_encoded_size(width, height, layout, options, metadata)
    }
    bound := pixels.checked(1, codestream_bound(width, height, layout)?, icc_bound(metadata.icc.len)?)?
    prefix := container_prefix(options, metadata.exif, metadata.xmp, bound, needs_level10(width, height, layout))?
    return pixels.checked(1, bound, prefix)
}

// Whether `icc` can be embedded for an image in `layout`: an RGB profile for
// RGB(A), a gray one for gray(+alpha) (see Metadata.icc).
pub fn icc_fits(icc: &[u8], layout: &pixels.Layout) -> bool {
    color_channels := 1usize
    if layout.channel_count() >= 3 {
        color_channels = 3
    }
    match check_icc(icc, color_channels) {
        ok() => {
            return true
        }
        err(_) => {
            return false
        }
    }
}

// Whether encode_with_metadata() accepts `icc` for an image in `layout`
// with these options: icc_fits(), and for lossy encoding a matrix/TRC or
// gray TRC profile (see Metadata.icc).
pub fn icc_usable(icc: &[u8], layout: &pixels.Layout, options: &EncodeOptions) -> bool {
    if !icc_fits(icc, layout) {
        return false
    }
    if !options.is_lossy() {
        return true
    }
    color_channels := 1usize
    if layout.channel_count() >= 3 {
        color_channels = 3
    }
    return vd_icc_usable(icc, color_channels)
}

// Scratch sizes in elements.
fn plane_words(width: u32, height: u32, layout: &pixels.Layout) -> usize {
    gw := width as usize
    if gw > 256 {
        gw = 256
    }
    gh := height as usize
    if gh > 256 {
        gh = 256
    }
    return layout.channel_count() * gw * gh + 4 * MAX_PALETTE
}

const HIST_WORDS: usize = MAX_CONTEXTS * MAX_ALPHA
const SUM_WORDS: usize = MAX_CLUSTERS * MAX_ALPHA
const ANS_WORDS: usize = MAX_CLUSTERS * ANS_STRIDE

// Effort 2 and up may code with ANS: they need ANS tables and a token
// buffer for the largest stream.
fn uses_ans(options: &EncodeOptions) -> bool {
    return options.effort >= 2
}

// Bytes of scratch encode() needs for this image and options.
pub fn encode_scratch_size(width: u32, height: u32, layout: &pixels.Layout, options: &EncodeOptions) -> usize!pixels.Error {
    if options.is_lossy() {
        return vd_scratch_size(width, height, layout, options)
    }
    check_size(width, height)?
    total := scratch.size(plane_words(width, height, layout), 4)?
    total = scratch.add(total, scratch.size(HIST_WORDS, 4)?)?
    total = scratch.add(total, scratch.size(SUM_WORDS, 4)?)?
    total = scratch.add(total, scratch.size(MAX_CONTEXTS, 4)?)?
    total = scratch.add(total, scratch.size(SUM_WORDS, 2)?)?
    total = scratch.add(total, scratch.size(SUM_WORDS + MAX_CONTEXTS, 1)?)?
    total = scratch.add(total, scratch.size(PALETTE_WORDS, 4)?)?
    total = scratch.add(total, scratch.size(toc_entries(width as usize, height as usize), 4)?)?
    if uses_ans(options) {
        total = scratch.add(total, scratch.size(ANS_WORDS, 2)?)?
        total = scratch.add(total, scratch.size(2 * plane_words(width, height, layout), 4)?)?
    }
    return ok(total)
}

// Encode `source` as a lossless JPEG XL file into `output`, returning the
// byte count. Fails with BufferTooSmall when `scratch` is shorter than
// encode_scratch_size() or the output does not fit, and Malformed for an
// empty image.
pub fn encode(source: &pixels.View, options: &EncodeOptions, output: &mut[u8], scratch_bytes: &mut[u8]) -> usize!pixels.Error {
    md := Metadata.new(b"", b"")
    return encode_boxes(source, options, &md, output, scratch_bytes)
}

// encode() with EXIF and/or XMP boxes and/or an ICC profile; the output
// uses the container when EXIF or XMP is present. Size the output with
// max_encoded_size_with_metadata(). An ICC profile that does not match the
// image's color channels (RGB or gray), or that lossy encoding cannot
// convert from, gives Unsupported (see icc_usable()).
pub fn encode_with_metadata(source: &pixels.View, options: &EncodeOptions, metadata: &Metadata, output: &mut[u8], scratch_bytes: &mut[u8]) -> usize!pixels.Error {
    return encode_boxes(source, options, metadata, output, scratch_bytes)
}

fn encode_boxes(source: &pixels.View, options: &EncodeOptions, metadata: &Metadata, output: &mut[u8], scratch_bytes: &mut[u8]) -> usize!pixels.Error {
    exif := metadata.exif
    xmp := metadata.xmp
    icc := metadata.icc
    if options.is_lossy() {
        return vd_encode(source, options, metadata, output, scratch_bytes)
    }
    width := source.width()
    height := source.height()
    layout := source.layout()
    check_size(width, height)?
    need := encode_scratch_size(width, height, layout, options)?
    if scratch_bytes.len < need {
        return err(pixels.Error.BufferTooSmall)
    }
    let slice.SplitMut { left: plane_bytes, right: rest1 } = scratch.split(scratch_bytes, scratch.size(plane_words(width, height, layout), 4)?)?
    let slice.SplitMut { left: hist_bytes, right: rest2 } = scratch.split(rest1, scratch.size(HIST_WORDS, 4)?)?
    let slice.SplitMut { left: sum_bytes, right: rest3 } = scratch.split(rest2, scratch.size(SUM_WORDS, 4)?)?
    let slice.SplitMut { left: choice_bytes, right: rest4 } = scratch.split(rest3, scratch.size(MAX_CONTEXTS, 4)?)?
    let slice.SplitMut { left: code_bytes, right: rest5 } = scratch.split(rest4, scratch.size(SUM_WORDS, 2)?)?
    let slice.SplitMut { left: small_bytes, right: rest6 } = scratch.split(rest5, scratch.size(SUM_WORDS + MAX_CONTEXTS, 1)?)?
    let slice.SplitMut { left: palette_bytes, right: rest7 } = scratch.split(rest6, scratch.size(PALETTE_WORDS, 4)?)?
    let slice.SplitMut { left: toc_bytes, right: rest8 } = scratch.split(rest7, scratch.size(toc_entries(width as usize, height as usize), 4)?)?
    ans_size := 0usize
    if uses_ans(options) {
        ans_size = scratch.size(ANS_WORDS, 2)?
    }
    let slice.SplitMut { left: ans_bytes, right: token_bytes } = scratch.split(rest8, ans_size)?
    let slice.SplitMut { left: lengths, right: map } = scratch.split(small_bytes, SUM_WORDS)?
    planes := scratch.i32s(plane_bytes)
    sums := scratch.u32s(sum_bytes)
    choice := scratch.u32s(choice_bytes)
    codes := scratch.u16s(code_bytes)
    words := scratch.u32s(palette_bytes)
    sizes := scratch.u32s(toc_bytes)
    ans := scratch.u16s(ans_bytes)
    tokens := scratch.u32s(token_bytes)

    plan := new_plan(width, height, layout, options.effort)
    if icc.len > 0 {
        check_icc(icc, plan.color_channels)?
    }
    level10 := needs_level10(width, height, layout)
    bound := pixels.checked(1, codestream_bound(width, height, layout)?, icc_bound(icc.len)?)?
    base := container_prefix(options, exif, xmp, bound, level10)?
    if output.len < base {
        return err(pixels.Error.BufferTooSmall)
    }
    shape := Shape { width: width, height: height, color_channels: plan.color_channels, alpha: plan.alpha, bits: plan.bits, float: plan.float, alpha_associated: plan.premultiplied, orientation: color.exif_value(&options.orientation), xyb: false }

    // The image header and ICC profile go first, while all scratch is free
    // for the ICC coder; the writer state is kept for the frame.
    header_pos := 0usize
    header_acc := 0u64
    header_count := 0u32
    header_overflow := false
    {
        w := BitWriter.new(output, base)
        write_image_header(&mut w, &shape, &options.color, icc.len > 0)
        if icc.len > 0 {
            let slice.SplitMut { left: icc_hist_bytes, right: icc_work_bytes } = scratch.split(hist_bytes, scratch.size((ICC_CONTEXTS + 1) * MAX_ALPHA, 4)?)?
            let slice.SplitMut { left: ring_bytes, right: rest9 } = scratch.split(icc_work_bytes, scratch.size(ICC_RING_WORDS, 4)?)?
            let slice.SplitMut { left: head_bytes, right: chain_bytes } = scratch.split(rest9, scratch.size(ICC_HEAD_WORDS, 4)?)?
            no_ans := [0u16; 1]
            icc_set := CodeSet.new(map, lengths, codes, &mut no_ans[..0], ICC_CONTEXTS + 1, true, ICC_MIN_MATCH as u32)
            if !write_icc(&mut w, icc, &mut icc_set, scratch.u32s(icc_hist_bytes), sums, choice, scratch.u32s(ring_bytes), scratch.u32s(head_bytes), scratch.u32s(chain_bytes)) {
                return err(pixels.Error.Unsupported)
            }
        }
        header_pos = w.pos
        header_acc = w.acc
        header_count = w.count
        header_overflow = w.overflow
    }

    hist := scratch.u32s(hist_bytes)
    analyze(source, &mut plan, planes, hist, words)
    tree := Tree.new()
    build_tree(&plan, &mut tree)
    tree_ctxs := [0u8; 2560]
    tree_values := [0u32; 2560]
    tree_tokens := tree.serialize(&mut tree_ctxs, &mut tree_values)
    contexts := tree.contexts
    if plan.lz77 {
        contexts += 1
    }
    // Effort 2 and up tune the hybrid integer configuration per cluster
    // from finely counted histograms and may code with ANS.
    tune := plan.effort >= 2
    ans_level := 0u32
    if tune {
        ans_level = 1
        if plan.effort >= 3 {
            ans_level = 2
        }
    }
    count := CONFIG_DEFAULT
    lz_base := LZ77_MIN_SYMBOL
    if tune && plan.bits <= 16 {
        count = CONFIG_FINE
        lz_base = LZ77_FINE_BASE
    }

    // Pass 1: count symbols over the whole image (again with the default
    // configuration if a residual is too large for fine counting).
    no_set_ans := [0u16; 1]
    set := CodeSet.new(map, lengths, codes, &mut no_set_ans[..0], contexts, plan.lz77, plan.min_length as u32)
    for attempt in 0usize..2 {
        for i in 0usize..contexts * MAX_ALPHA {
            hist[i] = 0
        }
        empty := [0u8; 1]
        dummy := BitWriter.new(&mut empty, 1)
        broken := false
        {
            e := Emitter.new(true, &mut hist[..], &mut tokens[..0], count, lz_base, plan.lz77, plan.min_length, tree.contexts)
            code_image(source, &plan, &tree, planes, words, &mut e, &set, &mut dummy, false)
            broken = e.broken
        }
        if !broken {
            break
        }
        if count == CONFIG_DEFAULT {
            return err(pixels.Error.Unsupported)
        }
        count = CONFIG_DEFAULT
        lz_base = LZ77_MIN_SYMBOL
    }
    // Cluster the context histograms and build the codes.
    limit := MAX_CLUSTERS
    if plan.effort == 1 {
        limit = 8
    }
    proj := [0u16; 288]
    projection(count, lz_base, &mut proj)
    set.ans = ans
    set.clusters = cluster_histograms(hist, contexts, limit, set.map, sums, choice, &proj)
    streams := 1usize
    if !single_group(&plan) {
        streams += plan.groups_x * plan.groups_y
    }
    if tune {
        set.build_tuned(sums, count, lz_base, true, ans_level, streams)
    } else {
        set.build(sums)
    }

    // Pass 2: write.
    entries := toc_entries(plan.width, plan.height)
    // First attempt: leave room for the largest TOC, write the sections,
    // then move them down behind the real TOC.
    reserve := 4 * entries + 1
    toc_start := 0usize
    end := 0usize
    overflow := false
    {
        w := BitWriter.resume(output, header_pos, header_acc, header_count, header_overflow)
        write_frame_header(&mut w, plan.alpha)
        toc_start = w.pos
        w.pos = toc_start + reserve
        if !write_sections(source, &plan, &tree, planes, words, &tree_ctxs, &tree_values, tree_tokens, &set, &mut hist[..], tokens, sizes, tune, ans_level, &mut w) {
            return err(pixels.Error.Unsupported)
        }
        end = w.pos
        overflow = w.overflow
    }
    toc_bits := 0usize
    for i in 0usize..entries {
        toc_bits += toc_entry_bits(sizes[i]) as usize
    }
    toc_used := (toc_bits + 7) / 8
    final_end := end - (reserve - toc_used)
    if final_end > output.len {
        return err(pixels.Error.BufferTooSmall)
    }
    if overflow {
        // The output fits only without the TOC slack: write again with the
        // TOC (sizes now known) in place.
        w := BitWriter.resume(output, header_pos, header_acc, header_count, header_overflow)
        write_frame_header(&mut w, plan.alpha)
        for i in 0usize..entries {
            write_toc_entry(&mut w, sizes[i])
        }
        w.pad()
        if !write_sections(source, &plan, &tree, planes, words, &tree_ctxs, &tree_values, tree_tokens, &set, &mut hist[..], tokens, sizes, tune, ans_level, &mut w) {
            return err(pixels.Error.Unsupported)
        }
        if w.overflow || w.pos != final_end {
            return err(pixels.Error.BufferTooSmall)
        }
    } else {
        from_at := toc_start + reserve
        to_at := toc_start + toc_used
        for i in 0usize..end - from_at {
            output[to_at + i] = output[from_at + i]
        }
        w := BitWriter.new(output, toc_start)
        for i in 0usize..entries {
            write_toc_entry(&mut w, sizes[i])
        }
        w.pad()
    }
    codestream := final_end - base
    if base > 0 {
        write_container(exif, xmp, output, base, codestream, level10)
    }
    return ok(base + codestream)
}

// LfGlobal (default LF dequantization, then GlobalModular: tree, codes and
// the global stream), the empty LF group and HfGlobal sections, and the
// groups, recording every section's byte size. Returns false when a value
// could not be coded with the counted statistics (never expected).
fn write_sections(source: &pixels.View, plan: &Plan, tree: &Tree, planes: &mut[i32], words: &[u32], tree_ctxs: &[u8], tree_values: &[u32], tree_tokens: usize, set: &CodeSet, hist: &mut[u32], tokens: &mut[u32], sizes: &mut[u32], tune: bool, ans_level: u32, w: &mut BitWriter) -> bool {
    section := w.pos
    w.write(1, 1)
    w.write(1, 1)
    if !write_tree(w, tree_ctxs, tree_values, tree_tokens, tune, ans_level) {
        return false
    }
    set.write(w)
    e := Emitter.new(false, hist, tokens, CONFIG_DEFAULT, LZ77_MIN_SYMBOL, plan.lz77, plan.min_length, tree.contexts)
    code_global(source, plan, tree, planes, words, &mut e, set, w)
    w.pad()
    sizes[0] = (w.pos - section) as u32
    if single_group(plan) {
        return !e.broken
    }
    at := 1usize
    for i in 0usize..plan.lf_groups + 1 {
        sizes[at] = 0
        at += 1
    }
    for g in 0usize..plan.groups_x * plan.groups_y {
        section = w.pos
        code_group(source, plan, tree, planes, words, g, &mut e, set, w)
        w.pad()
        sizes[at] = (w.pos - section) as u32
        at += 1
    }
    return !e.broken
}
fn write_container(exif: &[u8], xmp: &[u8], output: &mut[u8], base: usize, codestream: usize, level10: bool) {
    at := 0usize
    for i in 0usize..12 {
        output[at + i] = SIGNATURE_BOX[i]
    }
    at += 12
    for i in 0usize..20 {
        output[at + i] = FTYP_BOX[i]
    }
    at += 20
    if level10 {
        put_box_header(output, at, 9, b"jxll")
        output[at + 8] = 10
        at += 9
    }
    if exif.len > 0 {
        put_box_header(output, at, (exif.len + 12) as u32, b"Exif")
        binary.put_be32(output, at + 8, exif_tiff_offset(exif))
        at += 12
        for i in 0usize..exif.len {
            output[at + i] = exif[i]
        }
        at += exif.len
    }
    if xmp.len > 0 {
        put_box_header(output, at, (xmp.len + 8) as u32, b"xml ")
        at += 8
        for i in 0usize..xmp.len {
            output[at + i] = xmp[i]
        }
        at += xmp.len
    }
    if base - at == 16 {
        put_box_header(output, at, 1, b"jxlc")
        size := (codestream + 16) as u64
        binary.put_be32(output, at + 8, (size >> 32) as u32)
        binary.put_be32(output, at + 12, (size & 0xFFFFFFFF) as u32)
    } else {
        put_box_header(output, at, (codestream + 8) as u32, b"jxlc")
    }
}

// The MA tree: its code spec (six contexts sharing one distribution) and
// tokens. With `tune` the hybrid integer configuration is chosen from
// finely counted tokens and ANS is used when smaller (ans_level as in
// CodeSet.build_tuned).
fn write_tree(w: &mut BitWriter, ctxs: &[u8], values: &[u32], tokens: usize, tune: bool, ans_level: u32) -> bool {
    count := CONFIG_DEFAULT
    lz_base := LZ77_MIN_SYMBOL
    if tune {
        count = CONFIG_FINE
        lz_base = LZ77_FINE_BASE
        for i in 0usize..tokens {
            if values[i] as u64 >= FINE_LIMIT {
                count = CONFIG_DEFAULT
                lz_base = LZ77_MIN_SYMBOL
            }
        }
    }
    freq := [0u32; 288]
    for i in 0usize..tokens {
        t := hybrid_config(values[i] as u64, count)
        freq[(t & 0xFFFF) as usize] += 1
    }
    map := [0u8; 6]
    lengths := [0u8; 288]
    codes := [0u16; 288]
    ans := [0u16; 4608]
    set := CodeSet.new(&mut map, &mut lengths, &mut codes, &mut ans, 6, false, 0)
    if tune {
        set.build_tuned(&freq, count, lz_base, true, ans_level, 1)
    } else {
        set.build(&freq)
    }
    set.write(w)
    config := set.configs[0]
    if set.use_ans {
        records := [0u32; 5120]
        for i in 0usize..tokens {
            t := hybrid_config(values[i] as u64, config)
            records[2 * i] = (t >> 24) as u32
            records[2 * i + 1] = ((t >> 16) & 255) as u32 | (((t & 0xFFFF) as u32) << 6)
        }
        return write_ans_stream(&set, w, &mut records, tokens)
    }
    for i in 0usize..tokens {
        t := hybrid_config(values[i] as u64, config)
        set.put(w, ctxs[i] as usize, (t & 0xFFFF) as usize)
        w.write(((t >> 16) & 255) as u32, t >> 24)
    }
    return true
}
